discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** Concurrent `refresh()` calls from the watcher callback (line 47) and the polling interval (line 58) have no ordering guarantee — a stale poll read can overwrite a fresh watcher update.

Failure scenario: the poll fires `refresh()` which begins an async `resolveBranchName` (a small file read of `.git/HEAD`). A branch switch occurs while the read is in-flight. The reflog watcher fires and its own `refresh()` resolves first with the new branch name (e.g. `"develop"`), updating state and `branchNameRef.current`. The poll's earlier read then resolves with the pre-switch value (`"main"`). Since `"main" !== "develop"`, the dedup guard passes and `setBranchName("main")` overwrites the correct value. The footer flashes the wrong branch for up to one poll interval (5 s) — on the exact filesystems (NFS / FUSE / Docker overlay) that motivated the polling fallback.

```suggestion
    let refreshGeneration = 0;
    const refresh = async () => {
      const gen = ++refreshGeneration;
      const name = await resolveBranchName(cwd);
      if (!cancelled && gen === refreshGeneration && name !== branchNameRef.current) {
        setBranchName(name);
      }
    };
```

